        "title":  "Missed a lecture? This AI agent at Bar-Ilan University helps students catch up",
        "source":  "Microsoft AI Blog",
        "url":  "https://news.microsoft.com/source/emea/features/missed-a-lecture-this-ai-agent-at-bar-ilan-university-helps-students-catch-up/",
        "date":  "2026-10-15",
        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "Bar-Ilan University deployed a Microsoft Copilot Studio-based AI learning agent across 71 courses serving approximately 2,400 students, built on Azure AI Services by KPMG and OpenApp. The agent grounds responses exclusively in instructor-uploaded course materials — lectures, transcripts, and presentations — available in Hebrew, Arabic, and English, eliminating hallucination risk through constrained knowledge retrieval. Students reported study time dropping from 5-6 hours to 3 hours daily, and exam scores improved by an average of three percentage points.",
        "execSummary":  "This deployment demonstrates a production-grade enterprise agent architecture: knowledge retrieval strictly grounded in curated institutional content, with human-verified data sources and measurable outcome tracking. For customer-support and enterprise learning leaders, the replicable pilot-to-scale framework (71 to 171 courses) offers a concrete model for deploying AI agents against proprietary knowledge bases without hallucination exposure. The key architectural decision — constraining the agent to instructor-uploaded content only — is directly transferable to enterprise use cases like support KB agents or onboarding tools. The caveat: instructor upskilling and content restructuring are prerequisites, not afterthoughts, and should be scoped into any rollout plan.",
        "vendorLean":  "Leans Microsoft — vendor blog promoting Microsoft Azure AI Services and Copilot Studio",
