        "execSummary":  "A survey of IT leaders reveals a counterintuitive trap: the more advanced a company\u0027s technology stack becomes, the more entangled its dependencies and the harder change gets. Eight in ten organizations call themselves transformation leaders, yet nearly half remain hobbled by legacy debt — suggesting maturity scores are self-assessed and aspirational, not operational. For enterprise AI deployments, this is a direct warning: layering AI platforms on unresolved infrastructure debt magnifies fragility rather than resolving it. The implication for CIOs is to sequence remediation before expansion, not in parallel.",
